Commander Genius: the Games drawer
===================================

Commander Genius is an engine: it plays the Commander Keen games, but it
has none of them. This drawer is where they go. It is empty: no Keen files
come with this port, because they are not ours to give away (Keen 1, 4 and
Dreams have free shareware versions, but even those may be passed on only
as their owners allow).

Put each game in a drawer of its own here, with all of its files just as
they came from the DOS game, for example:

  Games/Keen1/       KEEN1.EXE, EGAHEAD.CK1, EGALATCH.CK1, EGASPRIT.CK1,
                     LEVEL01.CK1 ... LEVEL90.CK1, SOUNDS.CK1, ...
  Games/Keen4/       KEEN4E.EXE, AUDIO.CK4, EGAGRAPH.CK4, GAMEMAPS.CK4, ...
  Games/KeenDreams/  KDREAMS.EXE, KDREAMS.AUD, KDREAMS.EGA, KDREAMS.MAP, ...

Commander Genius finds them by their programs (KEEN1.EXE to KEEN6E.EXE,
K1DEMO.EXE ..., KDREAMS.EXE), so the drawers may have any names. Upper or
lower case does not matter. A game can also sit one drawer deeper
(Games/Keen/Keen1/), no further.

What it plays: Commander Keen 1 to 6 and Keen Dreams, and many fan-made
mods of them. Upstream's README (README-CG.md) says these versions work
best: Keen 1, 2 and 3 v1.33; Keen 4, 5 and 6 v1.4 (EGA; not Keen 6 v1.5);
Keen Dreams v1.13 (EGA). Where to get them:
  - Keen 1 shareware ("Marooned on Mars"): the shareware archive of
    Invasion of the Vorticons;
  - Keen 4 shareware ("Secret of the Oracle");
  - the full games are sold (for example Steam's "Commander Keen
    Complete Pack", which has the DOS games' own files).

With no game here, Commander Genius still starts: its launcher shows an
empty list and tells you this drawer's name. Add a game and start it again.
